---
title: Core vocabulary
summary: skoro-core, the shared types. Ids, the error type, binding roles, continuous/discrete kinds, packing user data into tensors, and samplers.
order: 2
---

`skoro-core` holds the types every other crate needs to agree on.

```
{../../../../crates/skoro-core/src/lib.rs:1..21}
```

## Ids

Every node in a model has an `Id`, created by an `IdGenerator`. An `Id` is a plain, weak name: it
does not keep a node alive (see [Handles own nodes](../../design/ownership/)).

## Errors

Recoverable errors are `SkoroError` / `SkoroResult`. Mistakes a user can make at runtime (a
dimension mismatch, a missing point, a node still referenced) are errors, not panics.

## Kinds

A quantity is either **continuous** (it lives on a manifold and can be differentiated) or
**discrete** (integers, categories). The `Continuous`/`Discrete` kind tags keep the two apart at
the type level, and `any_tensor` erases the kind when both must travel in one map.

## Packing

`Packable`, `NumComponents` and `Cardinality` describe how a user's value (a vector, a matrix, a
rotation) packs into a flat row of a tensor. This is how `add_constant(EuclideanD(3),
&VectorD::new(..))` becomes a `[1, 3]` tensor.

## Roles

A `Role` is the label on a binding edge (`"residual"`, `"fisher_root"`, …). It lives here, rather
than beside the graph's edges, so that `SkoroError` can name one.

## Sequences

A compiled program ([Compilation](../compilation/)) is a straight line of steps over an array of
**slots** $s_0, s_1, \dots, s_{n-1}$, each slot holding one node's value. A `SequenceMutator` is one
step of such a program, described entirely by which slots it reads and which one it writes:

```
{../../../../crates/skoro-core/src/sequence.rs:1..4}
```

Step $k$ computes $s_{o_k} \leftarrow F_k(s_{i_{k,1}}, \dots, s_{i_{k,m}})$, where
$(i_{k,1}, \dots, i_{k,m})$ are its `input_indices` and $o_k$ its `output_index`. Programs are
ordered so that every slot is written before it is read. That is all the structure the derivative
passes need: the forward pass runs the steps in order, and the backward passes run them in reverse,
each step pulling a cotangent back from $s_{o_k}$ to the slots it read
([Differentiable operations](../operations/)). Operations and samplers are both sequence steps, which
is why the trait lives here, below both.
